# Ethical Implications of Digital Imaging in Photojournalism.

**Authors:** Terry, Danal, Lasorsa, Dominic L.

## Abstract
Arguing that the news media are about to adopt digital imaging systems that will have far-reaching implications for the practice of journalism, this paper discusses how the news media is expected to adopt the new technology and explains why the marriage of journalism and digital imaging will create ethical issues with respect to photo manipulation that need to be resolved. The paper makes several recommendations for photographers and journalists. Reference citations are included. (RS)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED310397

